LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.

Ask Git for GIT_SHELL_PATH on Windows so core.shell and runtime prefix
resolution stay authoritative. Preserve its Unicode/spaced path as a single
executable name, normalize path separators, and propagate lookup errors.
Never substitute inherited SHELL or a host sh. Non-Windows keeps normal sh.
Serialize and cache the result for the current working directory and cached
subprocess environment generation; clone directory changes and environment
resets invalidate it. Preserve command quoting and existing process lifecycle.

Propagate errors through custom transfers and both SSH authentication and
transfer construction. Remove incidental formatter/sh-wiring tests, retaining
independent quoting, SSH option, multiplexing, and injection-security contracts.
This patch does not change the upstream Version constant or license files.
Apply with git apply -p1 in the extracted same-version vendor source root.
---

diff --git a/lfshttp/ssh.go b/lfshttp/ssh.go
index 01e3202..e0f6ba1 100644
--- a/lfshttp/ssh.go
+++ b/lfshttp/ssh.go
@@ -145,7 +145,10 @@ func (c *sshAuthClient) Resolve(e Endpoint, method string) (sshAuthResponse, err
 		return res, nil
 	}
 
-	exe, args, _, _ := ssh.GetLFSExeAndArgs(c.os, c.git, &e.SSHMetadata, "git-lfs-authenticate", endpointOperation(e, method), false, "")
+	exe, args, _, _, err := ssh.GetLFSExeAndArgs(c.os, c.git, &e.SSHMetadata, "git-lfs-authenticate", endpointOperation(e, method), false, "")
+	if err != nil {
+		return res, err
+	}
 	cmd, err := subprocess.ExecCommand(exe, args...)
 	if err != nil {
 		return res, err
